# Testing

Maximize confidence, not test count. Cover the behavior a regression would break, including one edge and one failure path when those can happen.

Choose the boundary that matches the risk: unit, integration, contract, API, browser, regression, or AI evaluation. Do not mirror private implementation steps.

A failing test should name the broken behavior. Avoid sleeps and order-dependent fixtures when a deterministic hook exists.

Do not delete or weaken a test to make a change pass without explaining the product decision. Tests that never fail under a broken behavior are not evidence.
